    "intro_html":  "Spanish albondigas have a trick worth stealing: rice goes inside the meatball, not just under it. That rice holds moisture, which is exactly what lean ground turkey needs to survive a week in the fridge. They simmer in a smoked paprika tomato sauce with a little cream stirred in at the end, and each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e565 calories and 35 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.93\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
